      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "How many bundles of shingles are in a square?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "There are 3 bundles of standard 3-tab or architectural asphalt shingles in 1 roofing square (100 square feet). Therefore, 1 bundle covers approximately 33.3 square feet."
        }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "How many squares of shingles for a 2,000 sq ft house?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "A 2,000 sq ft ground footprint home with a standard 6/12 pitch roof requires approximately 25 squares of shingles (75 bundles) once roof slope (1.118 multiplier), eaves overhang, and a 10% waste factor are included."
